  "question": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> are two hollow concentric cubes enclosing charges <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>Q</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>Q</mi></math> respectively as shown in figure. The ratio of electric flux passing through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is:</p><img src=\"assets\\qt0051_f9608775f560.png\" style=\"width: 290px; height: 290px;\"/>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mo>:</mo><mo> </mo><mn>5</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mo>:</mo><mo> </mo><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mo>:</mo><mo> </mo><mn>3</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo> </mo><mo>:</mo><mo> </mo><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Gauss's law states that the net flux of an electric field in a closed surface is directly proportional to the enclosed electric charge. Therefore,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>smaller cube </mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></math></p><p>Since the smaller cube is inside the bigger cube, so total charge contained by the bigger cube will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>Q</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>Q</mi></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>bigger cube </mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></math></p><p>Therefore, required ratio will be, </p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>smaller cube </mtext></msub><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext>bigger cube </mtext></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>.</p>"
  }
